[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue with one fix queued. Its own table says otherwise: the
reports in it come from three different bugs. The parser fix that is queued closes only the first.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Three problems, each with its own ticket. Fixing the parser leaves the other two open.
</Callout>

<Callout>
Closed. The three tickets are filed, counted and handed to the desk; this commit closes them.
</Callout>

## What is in #4471

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

The table counts the way the desk's own table on [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) does: each report goes
under the cause its tenant (locale and booking form) and channel give it, with the rules in
`#lib/kb/causes`, and each report id counts once, so the overlapping pages of the export do not
count twice. One-day moves come from `desk-notes.json`.

## The three problems

**`parser`: day and month swap.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant on
file writes the day first, so 7 April becomes 4 July. This is the bug #4471 names, and the queued
fix is for it.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form asks for the wrong order.** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its
date field. People follow the hint and type the month first; the form then reads the date the
tenant's way, day first. The result looks like the parser bug, but the parser fix does not touch
it. Only reports sent through the form of a booking-v3 tenant have this cause.

**`oneDayMove`: the date moves by one day.** These reports say Tuesday became Monday, or that one
meeting landed on Tuesday in Lisbon and on Monday in Toronto. That is not a swapped month. It
looks like a date shifted across time zones, and neither of the other fixes covers it.

## Why one ticket hid three bugs

- Triage merges on the subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  "Wrong day on the invite" fits all three bugs, so they all landed in #4471.
- Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant. A day-first tenant's
  staff on an `en-US` browser get tagged `hint`, and form reports get tagged `parser`. The table's
  first line says how many tags are wrong.
- [Triage: duplicate reports](/kb/triage/dedupe) and decision 0001 have not been reviewed since
  June 2024. The kb marks both stale.

## What the desk does now

1. Keep #4471 for the `parser` problem only, and link the other two tickets from it.
2. File new date reports by cause, with the dedupe explorer on the triage page, not by subject.
3. Do not mark #4471 fixed when the parser fix ships while the other two tickets are open.

